From: lzc256 <i@lzc256.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:44:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add pause/resume support to the voice recorder

The recorder could only start and definitively stop a recording session, so
there was no way to keep a single audio stream alive across an interruption
(backgrounding, a preview the user wants to extend, ...).

Add pauseRecord()/resumeRecord() to the VoiceRecorder API plus a matching
VoiceRecorderState.Paused: pausing releases the microphone but keeps the
encoder session (and therefore the output file) alive, and resuming appends
to the same Ogg/Opus stream. The recorded duration is accumulated across the
segments, excluding the paused time.
